Learned Counsel for the respondent cited the following passage from the Palmer's Company Law
(21st edition-1968, p.
334).
A transfer is incomplete until registered. Pending registration, the transferee has only an equitable
right to the shares transferred to him. He does not become the legal owner until his name is entered
on the, register in respect of these shares."
(1) [1969] (Vol. 73) I.T.R. 794.
